The model should support, as applicable:

- event identity;
- source/raw input;
- title/topic;
- nutshell;
- perspectives;
- learning;
- meaning;
- action;
- trust/provenance;
- connections;
- privacy/status;
- timestamps;
- reactions;
- rating;
- saves/favorites;
- Smart Lists;
- Smart Spaces;
- sharing state.

The renderer chooses the smallest sufficient section set for each event.

## 25. Accessibility

Premium must remain readable: high contrast, meaningful icon labels, adequate tap targets, visible focus states, no information communicated only through color, obvious selected/unselected states, and no motion required to understand content.

## 26. Non-regression / source-of-truth law

The **5:09 NayaNET Hub is the foundation, not the goal**. It is the proven house containing valuable shell, navigation, content, interactions, dimensionality, Naya presence, and feed ideas. Existing middle-feed prototypes are research/specimen material.

Keep what is genuinely right. Replace what is structurally wrong.

**509 FOUNDATION → FORENSIC INSPECTION → IDENTIFY VALUE → IDENTIFY DEFECTS → SURGICAL REPLACEMENT → VERIFY → ADVANCE**

Do not rebuild the whole house because one room is wrong. Do not preserve a bad room merely because it already exists.

